# The documents the character presents from.
#
# Somebody else's slides, usually, and large either way — nothing that lands
# here is ours to publish. The control server reads this directory while it is
# running, so a file saved mid-broadcast appears without a restart; see
# `--slides` and `src/server/decks.ts`.
#
# The directory itself is tracked, which is the point of keeping it here rather
# than behind a path somebody has to be told about: a checkout arrives with
# somewhere to put a deck.
#
# `hashidate.pdf` is the exception, on the same footing as `demo.yaml` next
# door: it is the deck the demo script presents from, it is about this project,
# and it is ours to publish. It is built elsewhere and lands here finished, so
# what is tracked is the artefact rather than a step. Keep it under the size
# `make check-assets` allows.
*
!.gitignore
!hashidate.pdf
